1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Marek Sobieski''' herbu Janina - magnat, wojewoda lubelski od 1599, kasztelan lubelski od 1597, chorąży wielki koronny od 1581. [http://pl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marek_Sobieski Wikipedia PL]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT (Research):Please be advised that there has been much controvery regarding this line. I have used readily available sources (in English) to assist anyone who thinks they might have this family connection. This chart is in no way c
2 CONC omplete, and is set here as a guideline or jumping off place. As all good genealogists must do, you must confirm your own charts through hard records such as birth certificates, death certificates, land records, marriage records, 
2 CONC etc. Some of this information may simply be lost, because of the many wars in Poland. This line is presented as an example. Thank you.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Sobieski Dynasty: Compiled by Margaret Odrowaz-Sypniewska, B.F.A., P.N.A.
2 CONT
2 CONT The name Sobieski is of Polish Origin. It means one who came from Sobieski, Sobieszki, or Sobieszyn (Sobiech's settlement), the namesd of villages in Poland (Smith, Eldson C. New Dictionary of American Names. New York: Gramercy Pu
2 CONC blishing Company, 1988). William F. Hoffman's book says that the root of this name ("Sob") means "self."
2 CONT
2 CONT John III Sobieski was the bearer of the Janina coat of arms.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their motto was "In hoc signo vinces." (Under this sign, you shall conquer) This rendering is from Herby Rodow Polskich
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
