1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teofila_Zofia_Sobieska
2 CONT
2 CONT Teofila Zofia Sobieska, née Daniłowicz (Polish: Daniłowiczówna) (1607 – 27 November 1661) was a Polish noblewoman (szlachcianka), mother of Jan III Sobieski, King of Poland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Zofia Teofila was the daughter of Voivode of Ruthenia Jan Daniłowicz and Zofia Żółkiewska, the daughter of Hetman Stanisław Żółkiewski h. Lubicz. Marriage and issue
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Voivode of Bełz and Ruthenia Jakub Sobieski h. Janina on 16 May 1627 in Żółkiew. They had seven children:[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT     Marek Sobieski – Rotmistrz, starost of Krasnystaw
2 CONT
2 CONT     Jan III Sobieski – King of Poland
2 CONT
2 CONT     Katarzyna Sobieska – wife of Władysław Dominik Zasławski and Michał Kazimierz Radziwiłł, mother of Karol Stanisław Radziwiłł
2 CONT
2 CONT     Anna Rozalia Sobieska – Benedictine nonne in Lwów
2 CONT
2 CONT     Zofia Sobieska – died in childhood
2 CONT
2 CONT     Stanisław – died in childhood
2 CONT
2 CONT     Stanisław Michał – died in childhood
