1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Euphrosyne (or Euphrosinia; c. 1352 – 1405/1406) was a Lithuanian noblewoman from the Gediminid dynasty, born as a daughter of Grand Duke Algirdas of Lithuania and his second wife, Uliana of Tver.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Marriage & Alliance:''' Around 1370, Euphrosyne married Oleg II Ivanovich, Grand Prince of Ryazan. Algirdas arranged the marriage as a strategic diplomatic alliance to strengthen political ties and extend Lithuanian influence
2 CONC  into neighboring Russian principalities (specifically Ryazan).
2 CONT * '''Grand Princess of Ryazan:''' As the wife of Oleg II, she served as the Grand Princess of Ryazan during a turbulent period marked by intense rivalries between the Grand Duchy of Lithuania, the Principality of Moscow, and the G
2 CONC olden Horde.
2 CONT * '''Later Life & Monasticism:''' Following the death of her husband in 1402, Euphrosyne took monastic vows (a common practice among medieval Eastern Orthodox noblewomen) under the religious name Eupraxia.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Information from genealogy Golitsyn -  Galitsine):
2 CONT * Yevfrosinia, died ca. 1405. Daughter of Gr. Duke Olgier of Lithuania.  Married: Great Prince of Riazanj, Oleg (d. 5th July 1402). 
