2 CONT >8.         MARIA [Agrafena]
2 CONT
2 CONT xx ([1350]) IULIANA Aleksandrovna of Tver, d/o ALEXANDER I Mikhailovich Prince of Tver, ex-Grand Prince of Vladimir & Anastasia [Iurievna of Galich] ([1325]-1392). 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT >9.         KENNA   
2 CONT
2 CONT >10.      JOGAILA [Jagiello] 
2 CONT >11.      '''SKIRGAILA [Skirgajllo] (-11 Jan 1397).  The Origo Regis Jagyelo records that "dux Jagello" granted "Poloczko" to "fratri suo Sergallo"[117].  He was baptised IVAN in [1383/84].  Prince of Troik 1382.  Prince of Polock
2 CONC  1387.  "Schirgalo…dux Lithuanie et dominus Tracensis et Polocensis" confirmed peace with the Teutonic Order by charter dated 1388, sealed by "domini Alexandri ducis Lithwanie et domini Kernoviensis"[118].  Prince of Kiev 1395.  P
2 CONC rince of Lithuania 1386-1392.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >12.      LENGVENIS
2 CONT
2 CONT >13.      KORIGAILA [Korigajllo] (-killed in battle Vilna 28 Oct 1392).  He was baptised KAZIMIERZ in 1386.
2 CONT
