1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =ADELHEID von Pommern=
2 CONT
2 CONT * ADELHEID von Pommern, daughter of BOGISLAW VIII Duke of Pomerania in Hinterpommern & his wife Sophie von Holstein ([1410]-after 1445) Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum records that “Hertoghe Bernd, Hertoghen Ereken son
2 CONC e to Sassen, unde eyn Here to Louenborch” married “Alheys, des Hertoghen dochter to Pomeren in der Slesye”[695]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * It is probably due to its great popularity that cities, islands and regions, such as the Australian city of Adelaide, were named after her in all parts of the British Empire. Thus, the princess from the small Thuringian Duchy ha
2 CONC d become a representative of world power No. 1. In Meininger Schloss Elisabethenburg the Blue Cabinet has been restored and furnished in her honor as a memorial site.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SAXONY.htm#BernhardIILauenburgdied1463A Project MedLands, SAXONY]
2 CONT
2 CONT
