1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 	Agata Czurlowna     Widow Of	 Teodor (Fedor) Danilowicz, Prince Ostrogski Living	 true Birth Date	 First Name	 Agata Last Name	 Czurlowna Gender	 Female Birth Location	 ,Lutsk,Volyn,Ukraine Manager	  Gerald J. Por
2 CONC ter
2 CONT
2 CONT Note by Natalia Gurko:
2 CONT
2 CONT =Agafia Czuryłówna was probably the wife of Prince Fedor Danilovich Ostrogski and the mother of the next generation of the Ostrogski princes.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Polish genealogical literature, she is known as Agafja, Ahafja or Agata Czuryłówna, and in Ukrainian literature also as Агафія Чурилівна Бродовська. Her exact origin has not been established by documents. Most genealogical reco
2 CONC nstructions are based on the charter of Czuryło Brodowski dated 8 April 1385, in which he gave the village of Brodowo to Prince Fedor and his children.
2 CONT
2 CONT The versions connecting Agafia with the Czuryłowie h. Korczak, the Gorajski family, or a particular Brodowski family are based on different sources and have different levels of certainty. A detailed study of the documents, histori
2 CONC ography, and the origins of these genealogical versions can be found in the Geni project “Agafia Czuryłówna Ostrogska: Origins, Sources and Genealogical Versions.”
