1 OCCU Received title of Count (Graf - DE) / Hrabia tytuł nadany
1 TITL count
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Piotr Komorowski, was appointed “Count of Liptov and Orava”, on Sept. 27, 1469 by King Matthias Corvinus of Hungary. His descendants took the surname Grocholski from their domain of Grocholice.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the expiry of his descendants, the title "Count of Liptov and Orava" was used by Piotr’s brother Mikolaj Komoroski and his descendants.
2 CONT
2 CONT Piotr Komorowski, Count of Orava and Liptov and former lord of the castles in the Orava region, was in 1474 deprived of his property by the Hungarian king Matthias Corvinus for forcing the Polish Prince Casimir of the Hungarian th
2 CONC rone. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Polish king Casimir IV for a reward granted him the loss of goods in Podkarpackie, including the castle Wołek. For the same 1474 years from the last written mention of the castle. Komorowski entered into secret agreements with the
2 CONC  king of Hungary, and the ability to enter land owned by him in the Hungarian influence was a threat to Polish. Piotr Komorowski died in 1476, and his property passed in the reign of his brother Nicholas, who refused to sell their
2 CONC  locks offer the Polish king. Casimir IV in 1477 sent troops under the command of Governor James Dębińskiego Sandomierz, which won the siedmiotygodniowym siege castles Komorowski. The king ordered to burn and destroy castles in Zy
2 CONC wiec and Barwałdzie [6] . Castle on Wołku was probably destroyed or seriously damaged during this expedition.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also see: http://pl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Komorowscy
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------
