2 CONC  Governor of Belz - 1499,  Governor of Łęczyca 1501r.,  Governor of Oswiecim
2 CONT
2 CONT Crown Hetman - 1499 - 1501 (http://pl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Piotr_Myszkowski_(hetman_polny_koronny)
2 CONT
2 CONT from wikipedia: Piotr Myszkowski was a Polish magnate and military commander. He was the Crown Field Hetman (1499-1501), Voivode of Łęczyca (from 1501), Voivode of Bełz (from 1499), castellan of Oświęcim (1484-1489), Wieluń (1489-
2 CONC 1494), Rozprza (1494-1497) and Nowy Sącz (from 1498).
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1499, the king of Poland, Jan Olbracht, made him the commander of Obrona Potoczna ("General Defense"), a semi-regular force charged with protecting the southern border of the Polish Lithuanian Commonwealth from Tatar raids.
