1 NOTE {geni:about_me} notę by Natalia Gurko:
2 CONT
2 CONT =Princess Anna Ostrogska
2 CONT
2 CONT Probable daughter of Prince Fedor Danilovich Ostrogski. According to the reconstruction of the Polish researcher Józef Puzyna, she was the wife of Jasiek (Jan) of Melsztyn, son of Spytek of Melsztyn, lord of Książ and Rabsztyn, me
2 CONC ntioned in 1410-1424.
2 CONT Puzyna names Anna as a probable daughter of Prince Fedor and states that she was married to Jasiek of Melsztyn, referring to earlier genealogical works by Wolff, Smoleński and Żychliński.
2 CONT
2 CONT As an indirect argument for this relationship, Puzyna also points to the connections between the Melsztyński family and Prince Fedor-Fryderyk Ostrogski, Anna’s probable brother. In 1438, Fryderyk acted together with Spytek of Mels
2 CONC ztyn, one of the leading members of the Polish pro-Hussite movement, against the estates of Zbigniew Oleśnicki, Bishop of Kraków.
