1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * https://lt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stanislovas_Glebavi%C4%8Dius
2 CONT Stanislovas Glebavičius (g. prieš 1449 - m. po 1513) – LDK valstybinis veikėjas, Merkinės vietininkas 1492–1495 metais, rūmų maršalka 1492–1511 metais, Vitebsko 1495–1501 m., Breslaujos nuo 1501 m., Polocko nuo 1502 m. vietininkas
2 CONC , Polocko vaivada (1502–1503, 1504–1513).
2 CONT
2 CONT research note by Natalia Gurko:
2 CONT
2 CONT Stanisław Hlebowicz of the Leliwa coat of arms (c. 1449-1513) was a statesman of the Grand Duchy of Lithuania, Court Marshal, Governor (Starosta) of Polotsk, and later Voivode of Polotsk.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is documented as Governor of Polotsk no later than 29 March 1501. During the early sixteenth century he played an important role in the political struggle surrounding the implementation of Magdeburg Law in Polotsk. Contemporary
2 CONC  sources describe him as strongly opposing measures that reduced the authority and revenues of the governor’s administration. His actions contributed, at least in part, to restoring the administrative situation that had existed be
2 CONC fore the reforms of 1498.
2 CONT In Ruthenian grand-ducal records he is consistently styled Governor of Polotsk until 20 October 1503. From 19 February 1505 onward he regularly appears as Voivode of Polotsk. The change reflects the reorganization of Polotsk provi
2 CONC ncial administration in 1505. Nevertheless, some Latin documents of the same year continued to refer to him as Capitaneus Polocensis.
2 CONT Latin forms of his title include:
2 CONT Tenutarius Plocensis - Governor/Starosta of Polotsk;
2 CONT Capitaneus Polocensis -Governor/Starosta of Polotsk;
2 CONT  Palatinus Polocensis - Voivode of Polotsk.
2 CONT His last known documentary appearance dates to 30 November 1513. He died in 1513.
2 CONT He was married to Zofia of Korczew (Zofia Korczewska), who survived him and was still living after 1537.
2 CONT
2 CONT A more detailed biography, including information on his career, landed estates, family, and inheritance, can be found in the Geni project “Stanisław Hlebowicz, Namestnik and Voivode of Polotsk.”
